id:                     E3554
trigger_tool:           interpreter|lisp|scheme|autotools|configure|require|init
phase:                  building|testing|consumer-run
error_signature:        Signal 11 \(core dumped\)|SIGSEGV.*no error|启动即崩|bad interpreter
severity:               2
category:               ohos, bisect, dummy-stub, graphics, headless
match_keywords:         without-x, dummygraph, dummy stub, nongraph, require, init.lsp,
                        spin-proto, depth-cuing, SIGSEGV, bisect, replacement runtime,
                        无头, 替代层, 桩
title:                  --without-x only switches the C layer; the runtime script layer still loads the dynamic-graphics stack and segfaults on dummy-stub dispatch — swap in the upstream replacement runtime (nongraph pattern) and bisect the require chain
root_cause:             configure-level headless switches compile dummy stubs (empty
                        implicit-int functions returning garbage), but the runtime
                        init chain (init.lsp) still unconditionally requires the
                        dynamic-graphics files; a message dispatch into a stub
                        (graph2.lsp: (send spin-proto :depth-cuing t)) consumes the
                        garbage return and segfaults deterministically. The device is
                        headless: no fix inside the stub is possible; the runtime layer
                        must be swapped to the upstream-provided replacement
                        (nongraph.lsp gnuplot layer) and the same require dropped from
                        downstream files (regress.lsp).
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           three-level prefix bisection along the runtime require/load
                        chain (init prefix -> loaded file prefix -> next require) using
                        exit-code counting with head -n prefix files, then an
                        idempotent in-recipe edit swapping the require for the
                        replacement layer; markers via captured output are unreliable
                        because SEGV drops stdio buffers.
rec_command:            head -n $k init.lsp > init.lsp && echo (exit) | ./interpreter; rc=139 => prefix contains the first crashing form
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-idempotent-init-edit
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      none-stub-is-unfixable
fallback_description:   Do not try to make dummy stubs return sane values; document the
                        dynamic-graphics commands as a platform hard limit in
                        notes/PR and keep the replacement plotting layer.
forbid_1_pattern:       # .*headless
forbid_1_reason:        Comments appended into Lisp runtime files must use `;`; `#`
                        raises `illegal character after #` and aborts the runtime load
                        mid-init.
forbid_1_consequence:   The replacement layer never loads and the crash returns in a
                        different guise.
forbid_2_pattern:       restore without md5 verify
forbid_2_reason:        Instrumenting shared runtime files (init.lsp) and restoring from
                        a .orig copy chain breaks silently; later probes then measure a
                        polluted input (observed false negative: 0/20 crashes on an
                        instrumented file believed to be the original).
forbid_2_consequence:   Wrong bisection baseline; conclusions do not reproduce.
affected_scope:         Interpreter/environment packages with configure headless
                        switches whose runtime init still requires the dynamic-graphics
                        stack, on devices with no display backend (OHOS PC); also any
                        "startup SEGV with no error output" where the crash happens
                        during auto-init before stdin is read.
verification_cmd:       prefix-bisect each runtime file with >=10 repeats of exit-code counting; after the runtime swap, full build + upstream suite + consumer harness must pass with exit 0
last_updated:               2026-10-19
authors:               unknown
doc_file:               doc/E3554.md
rec_description:        three-level prefix bisection along the runtime require/load
